# Test files and operator scripts must NEVER deploy.
#
# Vercel turns every `api/*.js` into a public serverless function. A test script or a one-off
# operator script living in api/ therefore becomes an internet-addressable endpoint that runs its
# body on every cold start, for anyone who finds the URL.
#
# This is not hypothetical. On 2026-08-14 TSC Roofing's site burned ~$12/day — roughly 12,000
# model calls — because `api/concierge-eval.js` was a test script in api/. Its body fired TEN live
# model calls at module scope and then called process.exit(), crashing the lambda into a 500,
# which is exactly what crawlers and retries hit again.
#
# The instructive part: that file was deliberately NOT named *.test.js, so it would not burn
# credits on every `node --test`. A correct instinct — and `.vercelignore` keyed on exactly
# *.test.js. The naming choice that protected it from the test runner is what exposed it to the
# internet. Hence BOTH rules below, plus the location rule (scripts live in scripts/).
#
# Doctrine: griffain-agency-workspace 06_operations/AI-ENDPOINT-GUARD-WALL.md
*.test.js
*.test.mjs
scripts/

# Internal records and infrastructure files must never be publicly downloadable.
# outputDirectory:"." serves the whole repo — everything not listed here ships.
# Found live 2026-08-20: touchdown logs, DB migrations (schema + RLS policies),
# internal review pages, and ops docs were all fetchable from the production domain.
log/
supabase/
internal/
*.md
SEO-IMPLEMENTATION-BRIEF.html
_v2c.png
package.json
package-lock.json

# The photoshoot MASTERS never deploy. They are the 4K originals every
# placement is cut from (scripts/cut-shoot.mjs) -- 6 frames that cost 240
# OpenArt credits. Archived as q95 webp so a re-cut never costs credits
# again, but outputDirectory:"." would otherwise serve all of it.
images/shoot/

# A look-only comparison page, never deployed (2026-09-25).
hero-forest-preview.html
